    "updated_at": "2022-05-04T05:45:05Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I think you're right about `eval \"$(pyenv virtualenv-init -)\"` being the culprit, because commenting it makes that line go away. However, `starship explain` doesn't tell me anything about that line:\r\n\r\n```\r\n❯ starship explain\r\n\r\n Here's a breakdown of your prompt:\r\n \"~/git/starship-venv-test \" (31ms)  -  The current working directory\r\n \"on ☁️  ca-production \" (11ms)       -  The current AWS region and profile\r\n \"❯ \" (<1ms)                         -  A character (usually an arrow) beside where the text is entered in your terminal\r\n(test-virtualenv)\r\n~/git/starship-venv-test on ☁️  ca-production\r\n❯\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnyway, `export PYENV_VIRTUALENV_DISABLE_PROMPT=1` apparently did the trick (as long as I put it in the `.zshrc` file; just exporting it in the current shell is not enough).\r\n\r\nThanks for the tip!",
